; Getting into the second part, which every test of it has to do first.
;
; The second part asks for the access code the first one prints, and until it
; is given nothing else happens. It is the same ten lines at the top of every
; script, which is what INCLUDE is for.
;
; This file has no TEST of its own on purpose: it is a piece of somebody else's
; script, and the name of the run belongs to whoever included it.

STEP "the access code the first part printed"
  EXPECT "Clave de acceso"
  INPUT  TIMACUS
  EXPECT "la puerta se cierra"

  ; And the door closing is the last thing before a pause, which the adventure
  ; asked for and which therefore waits for a key.
  KEY    SPACE
END
